      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785167290643,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "now data use means bandwidth use\nor server will take 200mb to transfer or serve\n",
      "fontSize": 13.290319955477145,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "now data use means bandwidth use\nor server will take 200mb to transfer or serve\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Asvh--TgaowawnpEOmqF4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1530.693282047886,
      "y": 729.9786321939376,
      "width": 225.19296264648443,
      "height": 311.56362622249003,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#ffec99",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1751468209,
      "version": 285,
      "versionNonce": 1212796799,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785166330904,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "now there is something called\nbandwidth pricing \nnow normaly What is bandwidth?\n\nEvery time someone accesses your\napp:\n\nHTML is downloaded.\nCSS and JavaScript are downloaded.\nImages are downloaded.\nVideos are streamed.\nAPI responses are sent.\n\nAll of that outgoing data counts\ntoward your bandwidth usage.\n\nFor example:\n\nA page = 2 MB\n1,000 visitors = 2 GB of bandwidth\nused.",
      "fontSize": 11.869090522761523,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "now there is something called bandwidth pricing \nnow normaly What is bandwidth?\n\nEvery time someone accesses your app:\n\nHTML is downloaded.\nCSS and JavaScript are downloaded.\nImages are downloaded.\nVideos are streamed.\nAPI responses are sent.\n\nAll of that outgoing data counts toward your bandwidth usage.\n\nFor example:\n\nA page = 2 MB\n1,000 visitors = 2 GB of bandwidth used.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "OzvyhCfqm2mbcTr6rsAlj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1292.70806476273,
      "y": 749.4789247658473,
      "width": 210.81860351562494,
      "height": 226.66666666666674,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#ffec99",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1964152831,
      "version": 389,
      "versionNonce": 2093191473,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785166956219,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "we have to pay\nsimply \nmore bandwidth\nmore pay in server\nbandwidth\n as compare to\ncloud storage\nprovider",
